{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "advection_2d_y_zero_grad_central",
    "description": "MMS driver: forced-steady linear advection along y on the unit box [0,1]x[0,1] with zero-gradient y-walls, discretized by grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D1y_zero_grad_bc (second-order centered interior, 2nd-order one-sided face rows). The y-axis analog of problems/advection_2d_x_zero_grad_central. Manufactured STEADY solution u*(y) = cos(pi y) — constant in x — held steady by the exactly matching forcing c * gy with gy = du*/dy = -pi sin(pi y): the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_y + c u*_y = 0, so u(t) = u* for all t and the discrete field drifts only by the spatial truncation of the y-operator. BC COMPATIBILITY (why cos(pi y)): u*_y = -pi sin(pi y) vanishes on BOTH walls (sin(0)=sin(pi)=0) — u* is genuinely zero-gradient-compatible — and its third y-derivative also vanishes there, so the rule's 2nd-order one-sided face residual is superconvergent (O(dy^3)) and the global drift is clean interior O(dy^2), mirroring the cos^4 polar-cap trick of problems/latlon_advection_meridional_zero_grad.esm. The one-sided y-operator is weakly non-normal, so the transport time is kept short (t=0.03, so c*t=0.03) to stay in the linear-drift regime where the observed order is a pristine 2 through NY=256. The x axis is PASSIVE: u* is constant in x, no x-operator appears, and NX is closed to 8 at the import edge; NY stays open (grid default 64, rebound by the convergence sweep). Geometry contract (grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm) fulfilled for the unit box: x0=y0=0, dy=1/NY (observed dividing by the metaparameter name NY per esm-spec 9.7.6), dx=1/NX. BUILD-TIME SCOPE CAVEAT (AGENTS.md): the free-name dy survives only in the runtime rule body; the ic, forcing observed, and test references spell y_j = 0 + (j-1/2)(1/NY) inline from literals and NY, never invoking the grid's y_coord free-name template.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:problem",
      "grid:cartesian_uniform_2d",
      "equation:advection",
      "mms"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Roache, P. J. (2002). Code verification by the method of manufactured solutions. J. Fluids Eng. 124(1), 4-10.",
        "doi": "10.1115/1.1436090"
      },
      {
        "citation": "LeVeque, R. J. (2007). Finite Difference Methods for Ordinary and Partial Differential Equations. SIAM. Section 2.12 (boundary-compatible manufactured solutions and one-sided closures)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "metaparameters": {
    "NX": {
      "type": "integer",
      "default": 8,
      "description": "Number of cells along x, closed to 8 here: the x axis is passive in this problem. Declared as this document's own metaparameter and passed down to the imported rule as the edge binding value, because esm-spec 9.7.6 binding site 1 has bindings flow DOWN only, so a name closed at an import edge is consumed by the imported subtree and does not re-enter this document's scope. The bare NX in the dx equation therefore resolves to this declaration, and the value folds when this document closes."
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Advection2DyZeroGrad": {
      "expression_template_imports": [
        {
          "ref": "../grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/rules/central_D1y_zero_grad_bc.esm",
          "bindings": {
            "NX": "NX"
          }
        }
      ],
      "variables": {
        "u": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Advected tracer field over the 2-D [x, y] index sets (constant in x in this problem)."
        },
        "c": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m/s",
          "default": 1.0,
          "description": "Constant transport speed along y; multiplies both the discretized derivative and the manufactured forcing, so the steady MMS balance holds for any value."
        },
        "x0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Left x domain edge (unit box): the grid's x0 free name (unused here; the solution is constant in x)."
        },
        "y0": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "m",
          "default": 0,
          "description": "Bottom y domain edge b = 0 (unit box): the grid's y0 free name (consumer-supplied geometry contract, grids/cartesian_uniform_2d/grid.esm)."
        },
        "dx": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "x-spacing 1/NX: the grid's dx free name; NX closed to 8 at the import edge."
        },
        "dy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "description": "y-spacing 1/NY: the grid's dy free name, resolved inside the rewrite rule's expanded body at evaluation. NY is the document-scoped metaparameter, substituted as an integer literal at load (esm-spec 9.7.6), so the convergence sweep keeps dy consistent."
        },
        "gy": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^4",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "description": "Analytic y-derivative of the manufactured solution: gy(y) = du*/dy = -pi sin(pi y). Constant in time and x; c * gy is the manufactured forcing that holds u* = cos(pi y) steady. Coordinates spelled inline from literals and NY (build-time scope caveat)."
        }
      },
      "equations": [
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "ic",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ]
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "y"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "cos",
              "args": [
                {
                  "op": "*",
                  "args": [
                    3.141592653589793,
                    {
                      "op": "+",
                      "args": [
                        0,
                        {
                          "op": "*",
                          "args": [
                            {
                              "op": "-",
                              "args": [
                                "j",
                                0.5
                              ]
                            },
                            {
                              "op": "/",
                              "args": [
                                1,
                                "NY"
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "u"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
          "rhs": {
            "op": "+",
            "args": [
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  {
                    "op": "-",
                    "args": [
                      "c"
                    ]
                  },
                  {
                    "op": "D",
                    "args": [
                      "u"
                    ],
                    "wrt": "y"
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "c",
                  "gy"
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dx",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "NX"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "dy",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "/",
            "args": [
              1,
              "NY"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "lhs": "gy",
          "rhs": {
            "op": "aggregate",
            "output_idx": [
              "i",
              "j"
            ],
            "args": [],
            "ranges": {
              "i": {
                "from": "x"
              },
              "j": {
                "from": "y"
              }
            },
            "expr": {
              "op": "*",
              "args": [
                -3.141592653589793,
                {
                  "op": "sin",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "j",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "NY"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "mms_steady_y_zero_grad",
          "description": "Manufactured steady solution u*(y) = cos(pi y) with c = 1. Derivation: the continuous balance is u_t = -c u*_y + c u*_y = 0 with u*_y = gy = -pi sin(pi y), which vanishes on both walls, so u* is zero-gradient-compatible and the one-sided face residual is superconvergent (see metadata.description); the discrete drift is pure interior O(dy^2). The t=0 assertion pins the ic wiring (reference equals the initial field). The t=0.03 assertion bounds the truncation-driven drift against the SAME steady reference (relative L2 far under the bound at the default NY=64; exact per-resolution errors pinned in tests/conformance/convergence/advection_2d_y_zero_grad_central/golden/errors.json). References evaluate at cell centers y_j = 0 + (j - 1/2)/NY, spelled inline per esm-spec 6.6.5 (build-time evaluation folds literals and metaparameters only).",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.03
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 1e-09
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i",
                  "j"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  },
                  "j": {
                    "from": "y"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "cos",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "j",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "NY"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "u",
              "time": 0.03,
              "expected": 0.0,
              "tolerance": {
                "abs": 0.001
              },
              "reduce": "L2_error",
              "reference": {
                "op": "aggregate",
                "output_idx": [
                  "i",
                  "j"
                ],
                "args": [],
                "ranges": {
                  "i": {
                    "from": "x"
                  },
                  "j": {
                    "from": "y"
                  }
                },
                "expr": {
                  "op": "cos",
                  "args": [
                    {
                      "op": "*",
                      "args": [
                        3.141592653589793,
                        {
                          "op": "+",
                          "args": [
                            0,
                            {
                              "op": "*",
                              "args": [
                                {
                                  "op": "-",
                                  "args": [
                                    "j",
                                    0.5
                                  ]
                                },
                                {
                                  "op": "/",
                                  "args": [
                                    1,
                                    "NY"
                                  ]
                                }
                              ]
                            }
                          ]
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                }
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
